verses.text:
“People of Benjamin, flee for your lives!
Leave Jerusalem!
Sound the ram’s horn at Tekoa.{a}
Light a signal fire above Beth Hakkerem.{b}
Disaster is peering down from the north,
and a huge wreck is on its way.

They treat My people’s deep wound as if it were small.
They say, “All is well, all is well,”
when nothing is well.{b}

“If you get worn out running with people on foot,
how will you ever run against horses?
If you only feel safe in open country,{a}
what will you do in the thick brush by the Jordan?{b}

Can anyone snap iron,
the iron that comes from the north?
Can anyone snap bronze?{c}

His burial will be a donkey’s burial.
Someone will haul his body off
and toss it outside Jerusalem’s gates.”{e}

Who has ever stood in Yahweh’s council{f}
and seen and heard His message?
Who has listened and paid attention to what He said?

Nobody argues for you in court.
A sore can be treated,
but you will not grow new skin.{d}

Yahweh appeared to me from far away.{b}
“I have loved you with a love that has lasted since long ago.
That is why I kept pulling you toward Me with faithful kindness.

So I cry out for Moab.
I wail for all of Moab.
I moan for the men of Kir-Heres.{h}

Yahweh says:
“Look, someone will dive like an eagle
with his wings spread wide over Moab.{j}

“Watch, a people is coming from the north,
a great nation and many kings,
stirred up from the farthest parts of the earth.{m}

“He made the earth with His power.
He set up the world with His wisdom.
He stretched out the heavens with His understanding.{f}

But I will pay back Babylon and everyone in Chaldea
for all the evil they did in Zion,
while you watch,” Yahweh announces.

“Come out from her, My people!{n}
Each of you, save your life
from Yahweh’s fierce anger!
